%% Owner: docs/02-architecture-overview.md — one question, from keypress to cited answer.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    box rgb(255,255,255) User / IO
        actor U as User
        participant UI as Streamlit UI
        participant API as FastAPI
    end
    box rgb(220,252,231) Retrieval
        participant R as Retriever
        participant RR as Reranker
    end
    box rgb(229,231,235) Storage
        participant DB as Postgres
    end
    box rgb(243,232,255) Generation
        participant LLM as LLM (Gemini, OpenAI-compatible API)
    end

    Note over U,LLM: Legend: white = user / IO · green = retrieval · grey = storage · purple = generation
    U->>UI: types a question
    UI->>API: POST /query {question}
    API->>R: retrieve(question)
    R->>R: embed question → query vector
    R->>DB: vector search + keyword search (SQL)
    DB-->>R: two ranked lists of chunk ids
    R->>R: RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion) → one list
    R->>RR: fused top-N chunks
    RR-->>API: top-k chunks, best first
    alt evidence is strong enough
        API->>LLM: prompt = rules + top-k chunks + question
        LLM-->>API: answer tokens (streamed)
        API-->>UI: SSE (Server-Sent Events): token, token, …
        API-->>UI: SSE: citations (chunk id, page, char span)
    else evidence too weak
        API-->>UI: refusal: "not found in the documents"
    end
    UI-->>U: answer with clickable citations
